        "narration": "Eighty million trees collapsed simultaneously without leaving a single crater. In 1908, a blind flash flattened eight hundred square miles of Siberian wilderness in a single second.",
        "visual_keywords": "misty forest aerial view"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Shockwaves rattled windows hundreds of miles away. Yet when scientists finally reached ground zero years later, they found no fallen meteorite, no impact pit, and zero cosmic metal.",
        "visual_keywords": "vintage research papers photo"
      },
      {
        "narration": "How do you detonate twelve megatons of force without leaving a trace? For decades, wild theories blamed anti-matter collisions, mini black holes, or crashing alien spacecraft.",
        "visual_keywords": "stormy dark night sky"
      },
      {
        "narration": "The true culprit was invisible because it destroyed itself mid-air. Supercomputer simulations revealed a hundred-foot stony asteroid violently vaporized six miles above the surface.",
        "visual_keywords": "3d digital graphic earth"
      },
      {
        "narration": "That high-altitude airburst unleashed a nuclear-scale atmospheric shockwave that shattered the forest below without the space rock ever touching the ground.",
        "visual_keywords": "bright sun clouds sky"
      }
